{
  "description": "The model route's shared cases (design/46-Model-Routes.md, \"The exact rules\"), replayed by rust/strata-ai/tests/route_cases.rs and dotnet/tests/Datalium.Strata.Tests/AI/ModelRouteCaseTests.cs on a fake clock starting at 0 ms. Not a wire format: it pins failover, health, hedging and the messages across the two engines. Each case builds one route named `r` from `candidates` in order, with `hedge_after_ms` (absent: no hedging), `breaker` ({failures, open_for_ms}; absent: none) and `accept` (absent: everything accepted; {reject_containing, reason}: an answer whose text contains it is rejected with that reason). A candidate has a `name`, a `provider` (its scripted client's provider name and so its health key; absent: `p-<name>`), a `model` (absent: none, so the request's is used), `ineligible` (a reason its eligibility check gives on every call; absent: eligible) and a `script`: one step per time that candidate is asked, in order. A step is `answer` (text; `finish_reason` content_filter makes it a refusal), `stream` (the updates' texts, then `break` to fail after them, or a `finish_reason`) or `fail` (`status`, transient or fatal as design/44's status rule says, or `error` `connection`, transient with no status; with `retry_after_ms` and `message`); `delay_ms` (default 0) is how long the client takes to answer, to fail, or to give a stream's first update (later updates follow at once). The scripted client answers with the model it was asked for, and usage 10 in, 5 out. The request names model `requested`. `calls` run in order, each started when the clock reaches `at_ms`; `stream` true calls the route's stream and collects it. `expect` holds `answer` ({candidate, text, model}) or `error` ({kind, error_type, retry_after_ms, message}: the route's own error, or the candidate's scripted failure as it is); `ends_at_ms`, the clock when the call returned (checked when given); `attempts`, every candidate's outcome from OnRouted, in declaration order; `hedges`; and `health`, the named keys' Snapshot after the call ({state, failures, until_ms when cooling_down or open}).",
